uniq - collapse consecutive duplicate lines

SYNOPSIS
    uniq [-c] [file]

DESCRIPTION
    Read from file or standard input and output one copy of each run of
    equal lines. Use -c to prefix that line with the number of copies. Sort
    the input first to group copies that occur far apart.

EXAMPLES
    sort names | uniq -c

SEE ALSO
    sort(1), wc(1)
